    <string name="settings_root_risk_title">About root mode</string>
    <string name="settings_root_risk_body">Root mode terminates TLS on this device: the app issues its own certificate and connects to the real server as a man in the middle. The certificate the client sees is therefore issued by this app, and the upstream (real server) certificate is no longer validated. This needs root, rewrites the system hosts file and installs a self-signed CA into the system trust store; disconnecting reverts all of it. An app that is already running may not see the newly installed CA until it is restarted once. Note that the hosts rewrite affects only apps that go through the system resolver; apps with Private DNS (DoT) or a browser\'s own Secure DNS / DoH resolve by themselves and bypass hosts, so this mode does not cover all traffic.</string>
