    <!-- The glass section. One master switch, **off by default** (the owner's
         call, 2026-09-27): a fresh install draws flat cards and the user opts
         into the effect. It replaced the old five-tier chip row
         (自动/关闭/低/高/自定义) — the tiers were a second and redundant way to
         say what the switch says directly, and "自动" (device-decided) was the
         one tier that made the section unreadable: the user could not tell what
         they were looking at without knowing their own device's RAM and core
         count.

         It was **two** switches (液态玻璃 / 磨砂材质) until 2026-10-01, when the
         owner merged them. The two halves of the material are unchanged — 磨砂
         is the *blur* (`DetourGlass.blurRadius`), 液态 is the *refraction*
         (`lensHeight`/`lensAmount`) plus the highlight and the lit edge — but one
         switch now turns on both, so refraction without blur is no longer
         reachable and every glass-on user pays for the blur.
         `resolveDetourGlass` records that trade-off. The two old labels survive
         only inside this comment: keeping either as a string would leave a name
         for something the UI no longer offers. -->
