    <!-- Data portability: export / import, plus the About entry.

         The export is deliberately a *settings* document, not a backup. It
         excludes the wallpaper image — a multi-megabyte photo the user already
         has in their gallery, and the one thing here that cannot be carried in
         a chat message — it excludes every piece of runtime state (the engine's
         applied settings, the cache-dirty repair flag, the schema version), and
         it excludes imported rule sources, whose content is a file on the device
         rather than a value that can be written down. What is left is a few KB of
         JSON that can be pasted into any chat app, which is the whole point: a
         backup nobody can move is not a backup.

         The imported sources are excluded in both directions and that is one
         decision, not two: dropping them on export keeps the file free of a name
         that means nothing on another device, and skipping them on import is what
         stops a restore from deleting the copies this device already has.

         Import applies each value through the same setter the corresponding
         settings row uses, so a setting cannot be exported without also being
         importable. That property is what keeps the two directions from
         drifting apart. -->
    <string name="settings_section_data">Data and about</string>
    <string name="settings_export">Export data</string>
    <string name="settings_export_hint">Save the settings as a JSON file (wallpaper image excluded)</string>
