    <!-- Battery-optimization reminder. Shown on every launch while the app is not
         exempt, and deliberately not recorded anywhere: the exemption can be
         revoked — by the user, by a ROM cleanup tool, or by the system after an
         update — so a stored "already told them" would go on being true after the
         condition it described had become false again. See `BatteryPolicy`.

         The body names the symptom rather than the setting, because "省电策略" is
         not a term the user has had to learn; what they can recognise is a
         connection that reports itself up while nothing loads. The hint exists so
         the window does not over-promise: only the exemption has an API, so the
         OEM-only 自启动 / 后台运行 switches are handed to the user rather than
         implied to have been checked. -->
    <string name="battery_title">Battery policy is not set to unrestricted</string>
    <string name="battery_body">The system may reap the tunnel while you are not using it, which shows up as a connection that reports itself up while nothing moves. Set speed\'s battery policy to \"Unrestricted\", otherwise background survival cannot be guaranteed.</string>
    <string name="battery_oem_hint">Some systems also need \"Autostart\" and \"Background running\" enabled separately. Neither has a standard entry point and this app cannot read them, so please confirm them in the system settings yourself.</string>
